    "title": "Shopping centre cluster analysis (mock exam, revision session)",
    "text": [
      "A cluster analysis was conducted on a sample of 899 consumers who visited a shopping centre over the past month. Customers rated the importance of (1) quality and variety of the retail offer, (2) centre design and architecture, (3) activities and events at the centre, (4) membership in the loyalty program on a 1–7 scale (1 = not important at all, 7 = very important). The survey also measured satisfaction (1 = very dissatisfied, 7 = very satisfied) and visit frequency. Table 1 shows average scores per segment, table 2 demographics and visit frequency."
